IMPORT prelude

-- Employment Agencies Act 1958 (Singapore) -- who needs a licence (ss 2, 4(1), 6), when a suspension or revocation takes effect and
-- what it stops (ss 10(4), (5), 11(1), (2)), registration and deregistration of agency personnel (s 12), appeals (s 14), offering
-- benefits to employers (s 16), engaging unlicensed persons (s 30), disqualification (s 32), the maximum penalties for the main
-- offences (ss 6(4), 9(2), 11(5), 12, 13, 16, 29, 31, 32, 33) and the cap on composition (s 41).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EAA1958.txt. The deposit says it
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and comes into operation on 31 December 2021; the only amending
-- Act annotated in the body is 5/2015 (s 36). The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is one out of step with the body
-- from s 33 on; this file follows the body's numbering.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules an agency, its staff, an
-- employer using an agency, and the Commissioner actually meet. Not encoded: appointment of officers (s 3), exemption orders (s 4(2)-(4)),
-- licence application and security (ss 7, 8), late renewal (s 9(3), (4)), registration cards beyond their penalties (s 13), the
-- inspectors' investigation and arrest powers (ss 17-27), vicarious liability (s 28), offences by bodies corporate (s 39), abetment
-- (s 40), registers (s 44) and rules (s 45). The prescribed fees and the prescribed manner of verifying a licence are in rules that
-- were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Employment Agencies Act 1958 -- licensing`

§§ `2, 4(1), 6 -- who needs a licence`

-- s 2: "employment agency" means any agency or registry carried on "(whether for the purpose of gain or reward or not)" for or in
-- connection with the employment of persons, "but does not include any registry set up by an employer for the sole purpose of
-- recruiting persons for employment on the employer's own behalf".
-- s 4(1): "Nothing in this Act applies to any employment agency wholly maintained or wholly managed by any department of the Government."
-- s 6(1): a person must not carry on an employment agency unless the holder of a licence. (2): a person must not perform any work or
-- activity in Singapore for or in connection with the employment of persons (whether or not to be employed within or outside
-- Singapore), on the person's own behalf or for an agency carried on outside Singapore, unless licensed. (3): (2) does not apply to
-- (a) a licensee; (b) a person doing the work "in that person's capacity as an employment agency personnel and who is registered under
-- section 12"; (c) a person doing it "for the sole purpose of recruiting persons for employment on that person's own behalf".
-- Exemption orders under s 4(2) are not modelled (the field is there so the case can be stated).
DECLARE Actor HAS
    `runs an agency or registry for employing others` IS A BOOLEAN
    `does employment work in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `recruits solely for its own employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is wholly maintained or managed by a Government department` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is registered personnel acting as such` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is exempted by order` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carries on an employment agency` IF
    `the actor`'s `runs an agency or registry for employing others` AND (NOT `the actor`'s `recruits solely for its own employment`)

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act is out of the picture` IF
    `the actor`'s `is wholly maintained or managed by a Government department` OR `the actor`'s `is exempted by order`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contravenes s 6(1)` IF
    (NOT `the Act is out of the picture` `the actor`) AND `carries on an employment agency` `the actor` AND (NOT `the actor`'s `holds a licence`)

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contravenes s 6(2)` IF
        (NOT `the Act is out of the picture` `the actor`)
    AND `the actor`'s `does employment work in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `the actor`'s `holds a licence`)
    AND (NOT `the actor`'s `is registered personnel acting as such`)
    AND (NOT `the actor`'s `recruits solely for its own employment`)

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the s 6(4) offence` IF
    `contravenes s 6(1)` `the actor` OR `contravenes s 6(2)` `the actor`

§§ `6(4), 9(2), 11(5), 12, 13, 16, 29, 31, 32, 33 -- maximum penalties`

-- s 6(4), 9(2), 11(5), 31(2): fine not exceeding $80,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both; second or subsequent conviction
-- (s 31: offence) $160,000 or 4 years. s 12(6), (7), (11), 16(2), 32(3), 33(4), (5): $5,000 or 6 months. s 13(2), 29, 33(2): $15,000
-- or 12 months. s 13(3): $1,000; second or subsequent offence $2,000 or 6 months. s 33(1): $5,000; second or subsequent $5,000 or
-- 6 months. s 33(3): $2,000; second or subsequent $5,000 or 6 months. s 30(1) is per employee and is dealt with separately below.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `unlicensed agency or work (s 6)`
    `operating after the licence expired (s 9(2))`
    `breaching a suspension, revocation or direction (s 11(5))`
    `failing to register personnel (s 12(6))`
    `working while unregistered (s 12(7))`
    `failing to deregister (s 12(11))`
    `forging or misusing a registration card (s 13(2))`
    `failing to issue a registration card (s 13(3))`
    `offering a benefit to an employer (s 16)`
    `false information to the Commissioner (s 29)`
    `work pass application for an unlicensed person (s 31)`
    `acting while disqualified (s 32)`
    `overcharging (s 33(1))`
    `false information about employment (s 33(2))`
    `inducing an employer to shun outside candidates (s 33(3))`
    `obstructing an inspector (s 33(4))`
    `breaching a licence condition (s 33(5))`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed agency or work (s 6)` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 160000 ELSE 80000
    WHEN `operating after the licence expired (s 9(2))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 160000 ELSE 80000
    WHEN `breaching a suspension, revocation or direction (s 11(5))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 160000 ELSE 80000
    WHEN `work pass application for an unlicensed person (s 31)` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 160000 ELSE 80000
    WHEN `forging or misusing a registration card (s 13(2))` THEN 15000
    WHEN `false information to the Commissioner (s 29)` THEN 15000
    WHEN `false information about employment (s 33(2))` THEN 15000
    WHEN `failing to issue a registration card (s 13(3))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    WHEN `inducing an employer to shun outside candidates (s 33(3))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 5000 ELSE 2000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed agency or work (s 6)` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 48 ELSE 24
    WHEN `operating after the licence expired (s 9(2))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 48 ELSE 24
    WHEN `breaching a suspension, revocation or direction (s 11(5))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 48 ELSE 24
    WHEN `work pass application for an unlicensed person (s 31)` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 48 ELSE 24
    WHEN `forging or misusing a registration card (s 13(2))` THEN 12
    WHEN `false information to the Commissioner (s 29)` THEN 12
    WHEN `false information about employment (s 33(2))` THEN 12
    WHEN `failing to issue a registration card (s 13(3))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 6 ELSE 0
    WHEN `overcharging (s 33(1))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 6 ELSE 0
    WHEN `inducing an employer to shun outside candidates (s 33(3))` THEN IF `repeat` THEN 6 ELSE 0
    OTHERWISE 6

§§ `10(4), (5), 11(1), (2) -- suspension and revocation`

-- s 10(4): an order of suspension or revocation "does not take effect until the expiration of 14 days after the order has been served".
-- (5): if within that period the licensee gives due notice of appeal to the Minister, the order "does not take effect unless the order
-- is confirmed by the Minister or the appeal is withdrawn".
-- Reading "until the expiration of 14 days" as: in effect once more than 14 days have passed since service (an inference about counting).
GIVEN `days since service` IS A NUMBER, `appealed within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN, `Minister confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN, `appeal withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order has taken effect` IF
    `days since service` GREATER THAN 14 AND ((NOT `appealed within 14 days`) OR `Minister confirmed` OR `appeal withdrawn`)

-- s 11(1): once a suspension is effective the licensee "may continue to carry on the employment agency ... except that the licensee
-- must not enter into new recruitment or placement agreements". (2): once a revocation is effective the licensee "must immediately
-- cease". (5): contravening (1) or (2) without reasonable excuse is an offence.
DECLARE LicenceState IS ONE OF
    `licence in good standing`
    `suspension in effect`
    `revocation in effect`

GIVEN `the state` IS A LicenceState
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may serve existing clients` IF
    CONSIDER `the state`
    WHEN `revocation in effect` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the state` IS A LicenceState
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sign new placement agreements` IF
    CONSIDER `the state`
    WHEN `licence in good standing` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `12 -- registration of agency personnel`

-- s 12(7): a person who performs specified employment agency work "when that person knows or ought reasonably to have known that he or
-- she is not registered" commits an offence ($5,000 or 6 months).
GIVEN `did specified work` IS A BOOLEAN, `registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or ought to have known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the worker commits the s 12(7) offence` IF
    `did specified work` AND (NOT `registered`) AND `knew or ought to have known`

-- s 12(9): on an application to deregister, (a) where it is accompanied by the personnel's written consent the Commissioner "must grant"
-- it; (b) in any other case the Commissioner "may grant or refuse".
GIVEN `with the worker's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner must deregister` IF
    `with the worker's written consent`

-- s 12(12): a licensee "remains liable" for the acts of a person who has ceased to be engaged and continues to be registered as its
-- personnel, "unless the licensee has applied to deregister the person in accordance with subsection (8)".
GIVEN `still engaged` IS A BOOLEAN, `still registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `applied to deregister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee stays liable for a departed worker` IF
    (NOT `still engaged`) AND `still registered` AND (NOT `applied to deregister`)

§§ `14 -- appeals to the Minister`

-- s 14(1): a person aggrieved by a decision to (a) refuse to grant or renew a licence; (b) debar the person; (c) suspend or revoke a
-- licence; (d) refuse to register personnel; or (e) deregister personnel under s 12(10), "may, within 14 days of the date of receipt of
-- the notice of the decision, appeal in writing to the Minister whose decision is final".
-- Not on the list: varying or adding licence conditions (s 7(4)), requiring or forfeiting security (s 8), refusing a deregistration
-- application (s 12(9)(b)), and directions under s 11(4).
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusing to grant or renew a licence`
    `debarring an applicant`
    `suspending or revoking a licence`
    `refusing to register personnel`
    `deregistering personnel on the Commissioner's own motion`
    `varying or adding licence conditions`
    `forfeiting security`
    `refusing an application to deregister`
    `giving directions after suspension or revocation`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is appealable` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `refusing to grant or renew a licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `debarring an applicant` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `suspending or revoking a licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refusing to register personnel` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `deregistering personnel on the Commissioner's own motion` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `days since notice received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal lies` IF
    `the decision is appealable` `the decision` AND `days since notice received` AT MOST 14

§§ `16 -- benefits to employers`

-- s 16(1): a licensee or personnel "must not give or offer to give (whether directly or indirectly) to an employer or a prospective
-- employer, any sum or other benefit" (a) as consideration or inducement for employing a person; (b) for continuing to employ a person;
-- or (c) "as a financial guarantee related ... to the employment of a person". (2): $5,000 or 6 months.
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `to get the employer to hire`
    `to get the employer to keep employing`
    `as a financial guarantee about the employment`
    `for none of the listed purposes`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `given to an employer or prospective employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the benefit is prohibited by s 16` IF
    `given to an employer or prospective employer` AND
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `for none of the listed purposes` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `30 -- engaging an unlicensed person`

-- s 30(1): any person who engages or uses the services of a person without the licence required by s 6 in connection with the
-- employment of any person is liable "to a fine not exceeding $5,000 for each employee engaged through that person".
-- (2): not knowing is not a defence "unless the defendant further proves that the defendant had exercised due diligence"; (3): there is
-- no due diligence "unless the defendant had verified, in such manner as may be prescribed", that the person had a licence.
GIVEN `employees engaged through the unlicensed person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum s 30 fine` MEANS
    5000 TIMES `employees engaged through the unlicensed person`

GIVEN `did not know` IS A BOOLEAN, `verified the licence in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 30 defence succeeds` IF
    `did not know` AND `verified the licence in the prescribed manner`

§§ `32 -- disqualification`

-- s 32(1): a person who (a) is an undischarged bankrupt; (b) has a conviction (in Singapore or elsewhere) involving dishonesty; (c) has a
-- conviction involving human trafficking; or (d) has been a director of or concerned in managing an agency whose licence was revoked,
-- "must not, without the consent in writing of the Commissioner, act or continue to act as a key appointment holder".
-- (2): other personnel (not key appointment holders) are disqualified only on (a) a human trafficking conviction or (b) the revoked-agency
-- ground. (3): $5,000 or 6 months.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `undischarged bankrupt`
    `dishonesty conviction`
    `human trafficking conviction`
    `managed an agency whose licence was revoked`
    `no ground`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `key appointment holder` IS A BOOLEAN, `Commissioner consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is barred from acting` IF
    (NOT `Commissioner consented in writing`) AND
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `undischarged bankrupt` THEN `key appointment holder`
    WHEN `dishonesty conviction` THEN `key appointment holder`
    WHEN `human trafficking conviction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `managed an agency whose licence was revoked` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `41 -- composition`

-- s 41(1): an offence may be compounded by collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum
-- fine that is prescribed for the offence"; (b) $5,000.
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `x` AT MOST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap for` MEANS
    `the composition cap` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` `repeat`)
